Contributed fact files (`*.facts.json`) are written here by a family that asks a
legal question of its own. The directory is legitimately EMPTY in the shipped
state — and git does not track empty directories, so it vanished on clone.

Three consumers assumed it existed: factRegistry (tolerant — it treats a missing
directory as "no contributed facts", which is correct), factAdmission.test.mjs
and proveUniversality.mjs (both not tolerant — they write into it).

This file exists so the directory survives a clone. Do not delete it while the
directory is empty.
